-- title:
--   Measurable observed-history events reduce to prefix events on a fixed count cylinder
-- statement:
--   Let an observed history path be almost surely a measurable function of an earlier-interarrival prefix Z whenever the count at the observation clock equals n. Every event measurable for the natural pullback sigma-algebra generated by that history path then coincides almost surely, on the count cylinder, with a measurable event Q of Z. The proof extracts the measurable set defining the original pullback event, takes its preimage under the measurable prefix-to-history map, and transfers the event equivalence using the assumed pathwise equality. The actual Poisson history-to-prefix factorisation must be established separately.
